cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CANGREJO: High-Performance Open-Source OSINT & Forensic Link-Analysis Graph Platform"
message: "If you use CANGREJO in your cyber threat intelligence, OSINT, or digital forensics research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-03"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - osint
  - threat-intelligence
  - link-analysis
  - digital-forensics
  - graph-visualization
  - webgpu
  - zero-knowledge-encryption
  - cangrejo-de-oro
abstract: >-
  Cangrejo is a high-performance open-source OSINT, Cyber Threat Intelligence (CTI),
  and forensic link-analysis graph platform inspired by Venezuela's historic
  "Cangrejo de Oro" scientific criminalistics heritage. It features a tripartite
  CSR graph store, 60 FPS instanced WebGPU rendering, a 3-tier layout pipeline,
  live Pesquisa OSINT transforms, and Bóveda Cero selective Zero-Knowledge
  encryption (AES-256-GCM + AES-GMAC).
authors:
  - name: "Proyecto Cangrejo Contributors"
